(* At a call's own step, a limit of steps or of depth names the function called, at its line, then the call that made
   it, as Python names the frame being entered: in f, called from run. A self tail call, whose step stays in its frame,
   names its function too. *)
f(x) = x + 1
defn count(n)
  if n == 0
    return 0
  end
  count(n - 1)
end
run() = f(2) + count(3)
run()
